postmortems anchored to evidence, with trigger vs root cause, duration gaps and open questions.",[64,65,66,67,10],"postmortem","incident","outage","sre",{"slug":69,"kind":4,"description":70,"keywords":71},"pr","Opens a pull request with a short body that says why, following strict writing rules: no test plan, no file lists, no dashes.",[72,26,44,73],"git","writing",{"slug":75,"kind":4,"description":76,"keywords":77},"pr-address-comments","Pulls review comments on your PR, fixes what is actionable, and pushes, without ever writing to GitHub.",[26,44,78,16],"review",{"slug":80,"kind":4,"description":81,"keywords":82},"release-version-bump","Cut a release for one project in a monorepo: sync, bump only if needed, tag with the CI tag prefix, push.",[83,84,85,86,56],"release","version","tag","monorepo",{"slug":88,"kind":4,"description":89,"keywords":90},"review-pr","Reviews someone else's pull request end to end and writes the review as a local draft file, never posted.",[26,44,17,78],{"slug":92,"kind":4,"description":93,"keywords":94},"start","Pulls the default branch, cuts a named branch from your task description, and starts working on the task.",[72,95,49],"branch",{"slug":97,"kind":4,"description":98,"keywords":99},"test-feature-locally","Verify a change end to end before a PR: bring up compose, start the dev server, drive the touched flow with Playwright.",[100,101,102,103,104],"testing","playwright","docker","e2e","local",{"slug":106,"kind":107,"description":108,"keywords":109},"format-on-edit","hook","Formats and lints each file Claude writes or edits with the tools the project already has.",[34,110,111,112,113],"format","lint","prettier","eslint",{"slug":115,"kind":107,"description":116,"keywords":117},"guard","Denies merges, closes, secret reads, container teardown and shell rewrites of tracked files until you give the go.",[34,118,119,72,120],"safety","secrets","guardrails",{"slug":122,"kind":107,"description":123,"keywords":124},"pre-ship-gate","Refuses commits and PRs that mix moves with logic, add dependencies, skip tests or are too big to review.",[34,72,44,78,125],"size",{"slug":127,"kind":107,"description":128,"keywords":129},"review-chain","Blocks the PR skill until code-review, ponytail-review and comment-cleanup have run in the session.",[34,78,44,49],{"slug":131,"kind":107,"description":132,"keywords":133},"stop-check","Blocks the end of a turn while a changed JS/TS project fails its typecheck or related tests.",[34,134,135,136,137],"typecheck","tests","javascript","typescript",{"slug":139,"kind":107,"description":140,"keywords":141},"text-lint","Refuses PR, issue and commit text with dashes, test plan sections, tables, hard wraps or features framed as fixes.",[34,73,44,142,111],"commit",{"slug":144,"kind":107,"description":145,"keywords":146},"worktree-guard","Refuses edits in the main checkout while another Claude session works there, and points you to a worktree.",[34,72,50,51,147],"sessions",{"slug":149,"kind":150,"description":151,"keywords":152},"context-hud","mod","Context window and plan usage limits at a glance: footer gauges, a per-category pane, and a warning past a threshold",[153,154,155,156,157],"context","tokens","usage","limits","hud",{"slug":159,"kind":150,"description":160,"keywords":161},"context-meter","Shows context size and session cost in the status line, and warns once when the context passes a threshold",[153,154,162,163],"cost","status",{"slug":165,"kind":150,"description":166,"keywords":167},"gh-guard","Blocks Claude from posting GitHub comments or reviews as you until you give an explicit go",[26,115,16,78,118],{"slug":169,"kind":150,"description":170,"keywords":171},"read-guard","Caps unbounded Reads of large files and tells Claude how to read the rest",[172,153,154,115],"read",{"slug":174,"kind":150,"description":175,"keywords":176},"secret-redactor","Swaps secrets, emails and IPs in tool output and prompts for stable placeholders, and restores real values in tool inputs",[58,119,177,178,179],"redaction","pii","privacy",{"slug":181,"kind":150,"description":182,"keywords":183},"smart-typecheck","After a turn that edited code, runs the check script once in each package that was touched",[134,137,111,56,86]],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"item":1,"related":24},{"slug":2,"kind":3,"description":4,"keywords":5,"version":10,"html":11,"skills":12,"hooks":16,"files":17,"sources":21},"github-work","skill","Works through the open GitHub issues assigned to you one at a time, with review and test agents and one PR per issue.",[6,7,8,9],"github","issues","backlog","pull-request","1.0.0","\u003Ch2>What it does\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>github-work\u003C/code> works through the open GitHub issues assigned to you, one at a time. For each issue it branches, fixes, runs a review agent and a test agent until both are clean, and opens a PR that closes the issue on merge.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2>When to use it\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>&quot;Work through my assigned issues.&quot;\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>&quot;Go through my backlog and fix them one by one.&quot;\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Cp>It only picks up existing issues. It does not look for new ones.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2>How it works\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>Lists your open issues with \u003Ccode>gh issue list --assignee @me\u003C/code> and orders them by priority label (\u003Ccode>blocker\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>high-priority\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>medium-priority\u003C/code>), then oldest first.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Starts each issue from a clean, freshly pulled default branch on a \u003Ccode>fix/&lt;number&gt;-&lt;slug&gt;\u003C/code> branch.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Loops review and test subagents until they find nothing, then commits in the repo&#39;s existing style.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Opens the PR with \u003Ccode>Closes #&lt;number&gt;\u003C/code> and a short summary, and lets the merge close the issue.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Passes PR bodies through \u003Ccode>--body-file\u003C/code> or a quoted heredoc so backticks render.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2>Requirements\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>git\u003C/code> and the GitHub CLI (\u003Ccode>gh\u003C/code>), authenticated.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n",[13],{"name":2,"description":14,"argumentHint":-1,"invocation":15},"Use when the user asks to work through their assigned GitHub issues, iterate through their backlog, or resolve open issues one by one. Picks up EXISTING open issues assigned to the user, fixes each, and opens a PR that closes the issue on merge. NOT for finding new issues.","/github-work:github-work",[],[18,19,20],".claude-plugin/plugin.json","README.md","skills/github-work/SKILL.md",[22],{"path":20,"html":23},"\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">---\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">name\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">github-work\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">description\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">Use when the user asks to work through their assigned GitHub issues, iterate through their backlog, or resolve open issues one by one. Picks up EXISTING open issues assigned to the user, fixes each, and opens a PR that closes the issue on merge. NOT for finding new issues.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">---\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">Fetches open issues from a GitHub repository that are assigned to the user, then resolves them one at a time by creating a pull request for each.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\">## Issue Selection\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">1.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Fetch all open issues assigned to the current user:\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">   ```bash\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">   gh issue list --assignee @me --state open --json number,title,labels\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">   ```\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">2.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Process issues in priority order: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`blocker`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> > \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`high-priority`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> > \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`medium-priority`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> > \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`code-quality`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">/unlabeled\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">3.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> If no priority labels exist, process by oldest first (lowest issue number)\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\">## Per-Issue Workflow\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">For each issue, follow these steps in order:\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\">### 1. Clean state\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">-\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Find the default branch: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`gh repo view --json defaultBranchRef --jq .defaultBranchRef.name`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">. Do not assume \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`main`\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">-\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Ensure you're on the default branch with a clean working tree\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">-\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Pull latest: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`git pull origin &#x3C;default-branch>`\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\">### 2. Branch\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">-\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Create a new branch named after the issue: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`git checkout -b fix/NNN-short-description`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (e.g., \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`fix/922-csrf-protection`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\">### 3. Implement\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">-\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Read the issue description carefully: understand the problem, impact, and suggested fix\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">-\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Make the necessary changes to fix the issue\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">-\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Write or update tests to cover the changes\u003